{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b4c9a3e2-7f1d-4e6a-9c2b-tsconfig-nutrition",
    "name": "tsconfig — Nutrition Client API",
    "description": "This checkout's 22 nutrition-client routes (mounted at /api/v1, with the ROUTE constants already carrying an /api/... prefix — so effective paths look like /api/v1/api/v2/..., not /api/v1/v2/...).\n\n19/22 routes are real implementations verified against the live database (nutrition_sandbox). 3 (Scan Meal, Auth Refresh, Auth Module Token) are honest 501 stubs — they need infrastructure this partial checkout doesn't have (AI vision, cookie/session mechanism, partner SSO secret) — see their request descriptions.\n\nAuth is now FULLY AUTOMATIC: a collection-level pre-request script mints a fresh, valid tsconfig-scheme token before every request, using CryptoJS (bundled in Postman's sandbox) to replicate scripts/mint-tsconfig-token.js — same AES-encrypted inner payload, same hand-built HS256 JWT. You never need to copy/paste a token or re-mint one when it expires. It reads three variables from the active environment: user_id, jwt_secret_key, crypto_payload_secret_key — all pre-filled in tsconfig-local.postman_environment.json. If you have another request (e.g. a 'Client Login' call) that also writes to the token variable, don't run it in this collection — it will overwrite what this script sets and you'll be back to a mismatched token.\n\nMutating requests (Generate Plan, Add Meal, Update Weight, Update Water, Complete Assessment, Delete Meal) write to the live shared database — send them deliberately, not as part of a blind 'Run collection'.",
